;; Built-in theme presets. (theme <name> (<role> <fg> <bg> <bold> <italic> <underline>) …)
;; Roles: see core/theme.rs Role::token; colors: #rrggbb | ansi-name | default | N,
;; or the bare symbol `nil` for no color (transparent — resets to the terminal
;; default). Every override is this full 6-token form — a role's whole look
;; (fg, bg, and all three style modifiers) is one setting, not five
;; independently-optional ones.
;; The "default" preset is injected synthetically — no overrides at all;
;; ThemeRegistry::default_style already applies DEFAULT_BOLD_ROLES to every
;; theme with no bold override of its own — omit it here. Each preset below
;; repeats that same bold set explicitly so its look matches "default"; a
;; preset can add/drop entries to diverge.
